    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d829">

                <pb facs="0911" n="1745" xml:id="pg1745"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 652.119/1916</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Curaçao</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Messersmith</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Willemstad</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-10-08T11:00:00-04:30">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 8, 1918, 11 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received October 9, 6 p.m</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I have the honor to transmit the following from Consul of the United States at
                    Puerto Cabello: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>October 7. Spanish steamer <hi rendition="#italic">Villamanrique</hi>
                            desires permission to proceed from here to Barcelona via Venezuelan
                            ports and port in the Canaries subject to same conditions as in original
                            license which reads Habana, Puerto Cabello, Barcelona, dated September
                            27. Appears to be no objection to this change. Signed, Henry.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>Send reply to Consul of the United States at Puerto Cabello.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Messersmith</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
